msgid "aboutPrivacy"
msgstr "Looking up an ORCID iD sends it to pub.orcid.org from your browser. Looking up a DOI sends it to api.crossref.org, together with this site's contact address, and to api.datacite.org if Crossref has no record. Cloudflare, which hosts this site, counts page requests on its own servers, in aggregate, with no script or cookie in your browser. Importing CITATION.cff or .zenodo.json loads the citesync converter and a Python runtime from this site; the file is processed in your browser and is never uploaded. Nothing else leaves your browser: drafts stay in its local storage, as does whether you closed the getting-started checklist or copied a statement. Asks to co-authors and their answers are kept only in this browser, and go into JSON exports unless you untick that option. Sending a reply hands its link, with that person's name and iD, to the app you choose. Signing in with ORCID on an answer takes the co-author to orcid.org and back; the sign-in then travels inside the reply link and is kept with the answer, also in JSON exports. It includes the name on the co-author's ORCID record. Opening a signed answer, or importing a JSON file with one, fetches ORCID's public keys from orcid.org to check it."

